.TH CHIME 1 2026-10-09 "chime 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chime \- run a command, and chime when it ends
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chime
.RB [ \-\-name
.IR job ]
.I command
.RI [ argument ...]
.br
.B chime
.RB [ \-\-error ]
.RB [ \-\-message
.IR text ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chime
runs
.IR command ,
waits for it to end, and then chimes: the desktop's
.I complete
sound when the command succeeded, its
.I dialog\-error
sound when it didn't. It also rings the terminal's bell and shows a desktop
notification saying how the command ended and how long it took, such as
.RI \(lq "make \-j16 finished" "\(rq with \(lq" "in 4m10s" \(rq.
.PP
It exits with the command's own status, so it can be put in front of any command
in a script or an
.B &&
chain without changing what happens next.
.PP
Ctrl\-C reaches the command, not
.BR chime ,
which still reports how the command ended.
.PP
Without a command,
.B chime
chimes at once, which is useful at the end of a script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-name " job"
Name the job in the notification, so it reads
.RI \(lq "Deploy finished" \(rq
or
.RI \(lq "Deploy failed with 1" \(rq
instead of naming the command.
.TP
.BI \-\-message " text"
When chiming at once, what the notification says. Given a command, it names the
job, as
.B \-\-name
does.
.TP
.B \-\-error
When chiming at once, chime the error sound.
.TP
.B \-\-
The command starts after this, even if it starts with a dash.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command's own exit status. When it was stopped by a signal, 128 plus the
signal's number, as a shell reports it. 127 when the command can't be found, 126
when it can't be run, and 2 for an option
.B chime
doesn't know.
.SH SOUNDS AND NOTIFICATIONS
The sound comes from the first of these that works:
.BR canberra\-gtk\-play (1)
playing the desktop's sound theme; the freedesktop sound theme's file played with
.BR pw\-play (1),
.BR paplay (1)
or
.BR aplay (1);
and its bell. The notification is sent with
.BR notify\-send (1).
All of these are optional. Each is given a second, so a stalled audio server or
notification daemon never holds
.B chime
up, and none of them failing changes its exit status.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B chime make \-j16
Build, and chime when the build is done.
.TP
.B chime \-\-name """Backup""" rsync \-a ~/ /mnt/backup/
Back up, and get
.RI \(lq "Backup finished" \(rq.
.TP
.B make && chime \-\-message """Built""" || chime \-\-error \-\-message """Build failed"""
Chime from a script.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR notify\-send (1),
.BR canberra\-gtk\-play (1),
.BR pw\-play (1)
